 ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2},$ then\n${y}_{2}(x)={y}_{1}(x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{x}^{{\\lambda }_{1}}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}{x}^{n}.$\n\n- **Case 3**: If ${\\lambda }_{1}-{\\lambda }_{2}\\in N,$ then\n${y}_{2}(x)={b}_{-1}{y}_{1}(x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{x}^{{\\lambda }_{2}}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}{x}^{n}.$\n\nWe are given that the indicial equation is ${\\lambda }^{2}-4=0.$\nSolving for the roots, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =4 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe larger solution is ${\\lambda }_{1}=2\\ge -2={\\lambda }_{2}.$ Therefore, the first Frobenius series solution we take is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={x}^{2}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}.\n$$\n\nNow, since ${\\lambda }_{1}-{\\lambda }_{2}=2-(-2)=4$ *is* a positive integer, the other solution is given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={b}_{-1}{y}_{1}(x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{x}^{-2}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}{x}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere the constants ${b}_{n}$ are found by substitution." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362484 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362484 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362484 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362484 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362488 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362484 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362489 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362484 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362484 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362484 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362489 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362484 1080 #uuid "89d99491-7d27-5bdb-9df2-3ce357f71ce2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362485 1081 "{y}_{2}(x)={x}^{-2}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}{x}^{n}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362485 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [